  "operative_text": "Section 1 (R.C. 2923.11): \"Mass casualty weapon\" means any semi-automatic firearm designed or specially adapted to fire more than thirty-one cartridges without reloading, other than a firearm chambering only.22 caliber short, long, or long-rifle cartridges.\nSection 1 (R.C. 2923.17): (A) No person shall knowingly acquire, have, carry, or use any mass casualty weapon or dangerous ordnance. (D) Whoever violates division (A) of this section is guilty of unlawful possession of a mass casualty weapon or dangerous ordnance, a felony of the fifth degree."
}